  "premise": "Two hours after Operation Resolute Passage, the intact six-ship sealift is committed west through Hormuz. BLUE holds temporary air superiority but its first-line CAP is recovering, Wildcat 2 is lost, and Wildcat 1 is under repair. Iran's original airborne package was destroyed, but its coastal kill chain and all nine surface combatants remain operational after correction of the previous route-convergence artifact. The coalition is now authorized to suppress the named corridor-control nodes, not to conduct a general attack on Iran.",
  "blue_intent": "Lead with the MCM pair, keep the auxiliaries in two protected columns, use the outer escort lanes to defeat missile and surface attacks, hold Lancer at standoff until targets are positively designated, and preserve the fresh Tiger CAP for threats to the convoy and strike package.",
  "red_intent": "Use depleted eastern pickets to force early classification and weapons expenditure, then combine the western missile ambush with the intact coastal network against the logistics columns. Keep the Shahin reserve staged unless the crisis expands.",
  "escalation_constraints": [
    "BLUE preplanned shore attack is limited to Bastion 1, Bastion 2, Bastion 3, S-300 Site North, and Coastwatch 1.",
    "Pantsir systems may be engaged in self-defense or when directly protecting an authorized target.",
    "Bandar Abbas Strip and the staged Shahin aircraft are not preauthorized targets.",
    "Neither side is authorized to expand the operation beyond the Hormuz corridor."
  ],
